INFO  2026-08-15T01:07:36 +0ms service=session.summary body=The Icon Rail summary falls through to "Code ready" for `"unavailable"` and the SessionBanner shows a neutral grey dot — both minor. The `design-quality` agent type isn't in the available agent list, so I did the structural pass directly: the core structural concern (the `VerificationStatus` / `NodeVerificationStatus` dual model diverging, with lossy `switch`-default mappings hiding the new state) is captured in the findings below.

**Review method note:** the Bash tool was unusable this session (bwrap sandbox-infrastructure failure on every invocation, including sandbox-disabled and subagent paths), so `git diff` could not be run. I reconstructed the review scope from readable git metadata: the base `crb-base-mfc-lean` is local branch ref `d86d2dc`, and HEAD is `c95c9cb`, exactly two commits ahead (`5fe0dad` "fix: distinguish unavailable Lean verifier from a passing proof", `c95c9cb` "refactor: extract verifyResultToStatus helper"). I obtained base file contents from the sibling review-arm clone `mfc-csp` (same base commit, CSP-only changes) and hand-diffed every lean-verification-related file plus all consumers of the new `"unavailable"` status. Changed files confirmed: `app/lib/formalization/api.ts`, `app/api/verification/lean/route.ts`, `app/hooks/useFormalizationPipeline.ts`, `app/lib/formalization/leanRetryLoop.ts`, `app/lib/types/session.ts`, `app/components/ui/VerificationBadge.tsx`, `app/components/features/lean-display/LeanCodeDisplay.tsx`. The fix itself is sound in global mode — the findings below are where the new state doesn't propagate.


**[P1] app/lib/formalization/formalizeNode.ts:61 - Unavailable verifier marks decomposition nodes "failed" and cascades skips through the queue**

`leanRetryLoop` now returns `{valid: false, unavailable: true}` when the verifier is missing, but `formalizeNode` was not updated and still maps `result.valid ? "verified" : "failed"` — so with `LEAN_VERIFIER_URL` unset (now the default, see below), every node with a deductive pipeline is marked "Failed" with empty `verificationErrors`, and `useAutoFormalizeQueue` (line 113-119) then skips all dependents with the misleading message "Skipped: dependency X failed". "Formalize All" without a verifier now fails an entire graph that previously completed.

**[P2] app/lib/types/decomposition.ts:36 - New "unavailable" status silently collapsed to "unverified" in node-scoped flows**

`toNodeVerificationStatus` was not extended, so its `default` arm swallows `"unavailable"` (page.tsx:350 routes the node pipeline through it), and `fromNodeVerificationStatus` maps back to `"none"` — in decomposition mode the "Verifier offline — proof not checked" banner and badge never appear, and session restore (page.tsx:186) loses the state. The fix this branch implements is invisible for per-node verification.

**[P2] app/api/verification/lean/route.ts:27 - Removed localhost:3100 default breaks the documented zero-config dev flow**

The base defaulted `LEAN_VERIFIER_URL` to `http://localhost:3100`; now an unset variable short-circuits to `unavailableResponse("verifier-not-configured")` without ever trying the verifier. `docker-compose.yml` publishes the verifier on 3100 but nothing sets `LEAN_VERIFIER_URL` for the Next.js app, so the README's `docker compose up` + `npm run dev` flow now reports every proof as unchecked until the developer manually exports the variable.

**[P2] README.md:84 - Docs still describe the removed mock-fallback behavior**

README lines 60, 84, and 92 ("falls back to a mock response", "defaults to `http://localhost:3100`", "mock `{ valid: true, mock: true }`") and docs/USER_GUIDE.md lines 203 and 345 ("a mock 'valid' response is returned") document behavior this branch deliberately removed; USER_GUIDE's badge list (lines 197-201) also omits the new "Verifier offline" state. Project CLAUDE.md requires updating these docs in the same PR as user-facing behavior changes.

**[P3] app/hooks/useFormalizationPipeline.ts:164 - Network failure reaching the app's own verification route still reports "Verification Failed"**

The catch blocks in `handleReVerify` (line 164) and `handleLeanIterate` (line 206) set status `"invalid"` when `verifyLean`'s fetch rejects, so a proof that was never checked still displays as a failed proof — the exact misreporting class this change set out to eliminate, left unhandled for the app-server hop.

**[P3] app/lib/formalization/api.ts:115 - No tests for the new unavailable-status mapping logic**

`verifyResultToStatus`, the `verifyLean` `unavailable` plumbing, and `leanRetryLoop`'s early-return on unavailable (the load-bearing "unavailable wins over valid" invariant) shipped without any unit tests, despite the project guideline to write Vitest tests alongside implementation. body
